                        "form": "ayez sur-utilisé"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "a084639f-cf1d-4a41-970c-e9e211e96622",
                        "entry_id": "24c076d2-fbe8-361f-a8b7-d0ebc17746aa",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "surutiliser"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "14303c22-47ff-3b62-b72f-3e1aa0f97ad5",
                        "entry_id": "24c076d2-fbe8-361f-a8b7-d0ebc17746aa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Utiliser plus que la moyenne, ou excessivement."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6e8a03ef-f252-4f48-92de-780893db77e7",
                                "sense_id": "14303c22-47ff-3b62-b72f-3e1aa0f97ad5",
                                "text": "Contrairement à Gilles et Clint et plus près d’Emmanuelle, Hélène sur-utilise les connaissances théoriques anatomiques pour venir à bout de cette prescription."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5375c526-ebd1-40b9-a6c0-47ba3afd118e",
                                "sense_id": "14303c22-47ff-3b62-b72f-3e1aa0f97ad5",
                                "text": "Le mot a fait florès depuis la fin des années 1970, sur-utilisé, et qui ne cessera de l’être y compris actuellement, accompagné de celui du déclin de la nation."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "465ec783-015e-4f1e-8f6b-402191483bbf",
                                "sense_id": "14303c22-47ff-3b62-b72f-3e1aa0f97ad5",
                                "text": "Nous avons constaté que les panoramiques avaient tendance à être sur-utilisés pour des déplacements d’un objet à l'autre sans que ne soient prises en compte la nécessité, la durée et la longueur du mouvement."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5d5ef3f4-a071-4417-ae45-a53211f3d3c3",
                        "source_entry_id": "24c076d2-fbe8-361f-a8b7-d0ebc17746aa",
                        "source_sense_id": "14303c22-47ff-3b62-b72f-3e1aa0f97ad5",
                        "target_lang_word": "overuse",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "overuse",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "10173e26-9daa-33b6-ac6c-3cf72e7006a9",
                                        "entry_id": "7c71543f-6b58-3423-8d23-66f9f029c854",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To use too much of (something); to use (it) too often."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "230396e9-9060-4ca3-b85f-8e4e2cf6a3e7",
                                                "sense_id": "10173e26-9daa-33b6-ac6c-3cf72e7006a9",
                                                "text": "Another group argues that the diagnosis is being overused and that many of the diagnosed cases are iatrogenic, or unintentionally shaped or caused by the practitioner"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e17988fb-f91d-4eca-a476-3bd755460048",
                                                "sense_id": "10173e26-9daa-33b6-ac6c-3cf72e7006a9",
                                                "text": "On a summer visit back to the farm here where I grew up, I think I figured out the central problem with modern industrial agriculture. It’s not just that it produces unhealthy food, mishandles waste and overuses antibiotics in ways that harm us all."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ab4e51a9-f4ff-4451-8f3c-429a4edd10cb",
                                                "sense_id": "10173e26-9daa-33b6-ac6c-3cf72e7006a9",
                                                "text": "Therapeutic zeal is express in a number of ways, some of them quite obvious, others subtle. A therapeutic manner that is too self-assured and controlling is a dead giveaway. Other obvious signs of therapeutic zeal include getting annoyed or openly frustrated with patients who do not change in the way the therapist desires; \"blaming\" the patient by vidictively attributing lack of results to more severe pathology than was intially assumed; or overusing such terms as passive aggressive and poorly motivated."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "overuse",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d6f5a8e0-3bd4-30d0-874d-7c41f33f4e95",
                                        "entry_id": "b16ce8c1-bcec-3e9b-95a9-a461ac59e619",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "excessive use"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a9b6084-0428-4c41-abea-3402a789c481",
                                                "sense_id": "d6f5a8e0-3bd4-30d0-874d-7c41f33f4e95",
                                                "text": "There’s an occasional schmaltziness, aggravated by the overuse of a twangy score, but more than enough moments of genuine heartbreak, joy and suspense to make up for it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
